====================================================================================================
THEOREM E  (t = g(block index)):  strict geometric fibre design <=> g bounded
====================================================================================================
                 g  max g on [0,K)  #empty fibres   min(maxpre(m)-m)
            g == 0               0              0                  0
            g == 3               3              2                 -3
     g = k  (c=2j)              39             20                -19
          g = k//2              19             13                -13
      g = isqrt(k)               6              5                 -5
       g = k mod 2               1             20                  0
  g = 5 - min(k,5)               5              4                  0
  holes 0,4,20,100              80              0                -16

Reading: 'min(maxpre(m)-m)' is the worst log_b-deficiency of a fibre; a strict
geometric design needs #empty fibres = 0 AND that quantity bounded below.  Every
unbounded g in the table fails one of the two -- as Theorem E says it must.
